1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,385
Wait, That's My Hoodie.

3
00:00:03,385 --> 00:00:06,312
I'm getting ready to meet Emma when I notice something missing.

4
00:00:06,312 --> 00:00:08,958
My favorite green hoodie isn't on my chair.

5
00:00:08,958 --> 00:00:11,073
It isn't in my closet, either.

6
00:00:11,073 --> 00:00:14,021
Then a small green shape walks past my door.

7
00:00:14,284 --> 00:00:15,413
Morning.

8
00:00:15,413 --> 00:00:17,299
Nice weather, right?

9
00:00:17,572 --> 00:00:19,399
Wait, that's my hoodie.

10
00:00:19,399 --> 00:00:20,920
Ben stops.

11
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:25,107
The sleeves cover both his hands, and the bottom reaches almost to his knees.

12
00:00:25,107 --> 00:00:26,993
It looks a little big on you.

13
00:00:27,268 --> 00:00:28,772
That's the style.

14
00:00:28,772 --> 00:00:30,355
Very comfortable.

15
00:00:30,355 --> 00:00:32,418
Lots of room for snacks.

16
00:00:32,692 --> 00:00:34,457
I was going to wear it today.

17
00:00:34,457 --> 00:00:36,248
Did you take it from my chair?

18
00:00:36,532 --> 00:00:37,661
Maybe.

19
00:00:37,661 --> 00:00:39,119
Can I borrow it?

20
00:00:39,388 --> 00:00:41,952
You're supposed to ask that before you put it on.

21
00:00:42,172 --> 00:00:43,955
Everything okay in here?

22
00:00:44,188 --> 00:00:46,453
We're having a small fashion discussion.

23
00:00:46,453 --> 00:00:49,755
I need my hoodie, and Ben seems to be living inside it.

24
00:00:50,044 --> 00:00:51,840
I like the big pocket.

25
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:54,236
My own sweatshirt doesn't have one.

26
00:00:54,508 --> 00:00:56,835
Your blue jacket has two pockets.

27
00:00:56,835 --> 00:00:58,668
It's hanging by the door.

28
00:00:58,948 --> 00:01:00,369
Two pockets?

29
00:01:00,369 --> 00:01:02,358
That does change things.

30
00:01:02,644 --> 00:01:05,190
He pulls off the hoodie and hands it back.

31
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:09,773
I check the pocket and find a toy car, a clean tissue, and a tiny rubber duck.

32
00:01:09,773 --> 00:01:11,909
Please ask me first next time.

33
00:01:12,196 --> 00:01:13,294
Deal.

34
00:01:13,294 --> 00:01:15,086
Can I borrow it tomorrow?

35
00:01:15,364 --> 00:01:16,504
Maybe.

36
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:18,108
Ask me tomorrow.

37
00:01:18,108 --> 00:01:20,858
For now, your duck needs a new apartment.

38
00:01:21,124 --> 00:01:23,076
The blue jacket has room.

39
00:01:23,076 --> 00:01:25,055
He can have his own pocket.
